Authorship and AI assistance: all code and documentation are authored by the
project's human author(s), who hold the copyright. Generative AI tools were used
to assist with development. An AI system is a tool, not an author or a
contributor: it holds no copyright and makes no copyright claim, and AI systems
cannot hold copyright. This assistance is acknowledged here, not recorded as
authorship. An assisted commit ends with a plain line naming the tool used —
"Assisted by <tool> (<vendor>)." — never an authorship or co-authorship trailer.
